{"kind":"artifact","text":"SKILL.md at exact bf75a0afde3f843d68c44e7e63ef7d329abdbac9 on request/skill-simplify, under promise git:sha1…a431970 on request git:sha1…205421b\n\nSKILL.md now carries the loop and says to use it lightly; AGENTS.md carries only what this repository adds.\n\nConditions met, in the order the request states them.\n\n1. Verified against the code at this head, not from memory. Every command and\nflag the page names exists in cmd/gs at bf75a0af: work --next, wait, inspect,\npromise, reassign-if-unclaimed with its flags before the request, artifact\n(--head --promise --report --rests-on --text), review-request (--head --to\n--replace), review (--artifact --promise --checkout --verdict --text-file),\nland (--approval --checkout --text --cleanup), and state, batch, ratify and\nsupersede. `gs presence` is not a CLI command and the page claims none; the\nfour presence states and the eight-event focus limit are enforced at\ninternal/service/server.go:676 and host/live/live.go:728 and advertised at\ncmd/gitseq-mcp/main.go:704. `status.durable.vocabulary.definitions` is the\nreal path in the resident's status response. All sixteen document links\nresolve, including both anchors into merge.md and the four-facts anchor into\ndecision-authority.md.\n\nThe verification found one defect in the page itself. Seven of the twelve\nartifacts its front matter cited for the behaviour it describes had been\nretired by later merges, so the page stood on dead bases and could never have\nflared. The citations are repointed at the live artifact for each path at the\nnewest commit that is an ancestor of main: cmd/gs/main.go, usage.go,\nartifact.go, review_request.go, work_next.go and internal/workroom/fold.go\nmove forward, promise.go, land.go, preflight.go,\ninternal/app/request_authoring.go and internal/statusview/query.go were\nalready live and stay, and the second, older cmd/gs/main.go entry collapses\ninto the first. Eleven live bases where there were twelve, seven of them dead.\nThe docset gate passes either way, so it does not catch this.\n\n2. Shorter, with the refusal catalogues replaced by links. SKILL.md is 208\nlines and 1441 words against 213 and 1499; AGENTS.md is 40 lines and 275 words\nagainst 100 and 756. The pair an actor reads each cycle went from 2255 words\nto 1716. Every refusal list removed from a step was confirmed present in that\ncommand's reference page under its \"what is wrong | the refusal names\" table:\npromise.md:62, artifact.md:78, review-request.md:65, review.md:103, and\nland.md's ordered account at lines 84 to 102. No step lost a rule. Two rules\nwere added: check the evidence rather than the claim, and a gate you did not\nrun or did not read is not evidence.\n\n3. The drift is resolved towards SKILL.md. AGENTS.md no longer restates the\nloop, the worktree section, the presence definition or the ephemerality rules.\nIt names three rules this repository deliberately repeats, and says that is\nwhat they are, and keeps what is genuinely local: the superseded-world merge\nrefusal, the dot-artifact migration, and the presence policy.\n\n4. `make docs` and `make test` both green at exactly bf75a0af, exit 0. The\ndocset suite is the one that reads these pages, and Go had served it from\ncache, so it was rerun with -count=1 at this head: ok, 41.9s. The rest of\n./... reports ok from Go's content-addressed cache, filled when the same\nsuite ran fresh at a15234fa (cmd/gs 697.9s, internal/app 228.5s,\ncmd/gitseq-mcp 91.3s, internal/workroom 6.6s); no Go file differs between\na15234fa and this head, only SKILL.md's front matter.\n\n5. This set is the implementation report: one artifact per changed path, both\nresting on the eleven repointed behaviour bases.","body":{"commit":"bf75a0afde3f843d68c44e7e63ef7d329abdbac9","path":"SKILL.md"}}